      "message": "Count coverage in panels and tell activity by the day\n\nCoverage opens with one panel: the strip of what backs the branch, the\nlegend in counts, and the key under it. The burndown is a panel of its\nown. The files are rows in a panel, ten of them unless all are asked\nfor, each with its bar and its unjudged and total lines; a file with a\ntask or a covering claim says so under its name. The rail carries the\nverified share with its sparkline over the last tips, the pay-it-down\nform, and who paid what down, drawn by name.\n\nActivity is a timeline: rows grouped by day, each with the actor drawn,\nthe sentence, the session it happened in and the time, behind filter\npills for changes, reviews, claims, tasks and sessions, and the\nrepository itself. The forge-wide log on the operator door reads the\nsame, with the repository as a chip on each row.\n\nChange-Id: Icoverage0131\nTask: t-04yvavdef7tky5009qsfr3tvrm\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
